./architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/validation/review-rg.stdout.log:45:architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/scope-check.md:11:The core premise still holds after Wave 009: the repository contains a backend Express/file-storage project API with its own broad `any` project DTO shape, while the active frontend project lifecycle uses the Wave 004 command-stream `ProjectService` through the Wave 009 app-shell runtime and Google Drive ports. The only frontend/backend coupling found in active source is not a real API boundary; it is a direct TypeScript import from `frontend/src/components/dialogs/OpenProjectDialog.vue` into `backend/src/models/Project.ts`. The active app shell no longer renders that dialog, so the import leak is also attached to a dead/obsolete frontend component rather than a validated backend integration.
./architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/validation/review-rg.stdout.log:46:architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/scope-check.md:13:Recommended stance for proposals: prefer deleting the unused backend project API and the dead `OpenProjectDialog.vue` surface. A keep-backend alternative is still viable for review, but it must make the backend a real typed project boundary and add backend/root validation; it should not preserve the current disconnected backend plus frontend implementation import leak.
./architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/validation/review-rg.stdout.log:47:architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/scope-check.md:29:`backend/src/models/Project.ts` defines `ProjectDTO` with separate `elements2D`, `elements3D`, `dependencyGraph`, `planes`, `hingeLines`, `view2D`, `processTree`, and optional `commandHistory` fields (`backend/src/models/Project.ts:6-52`). Several central fields are `Array<any>` or `any` (`backend/src/models/Project.ts:13-14`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:43`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:50`). This does not match the active Wave 004 frontend contract, where `ProjectData` contains `schemaVersion`, `nextElementId`, and committed command snapshots (`frontend/src/services/ProjectService.ts:11-19`) and is validated as schema version `6.0.0` (`frontend/src/services/ProjectService.ts:24-31`, `frontend/src/services/ProjectService.ts:80-129`).
./architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/validation/review-rg.stdout.log:48:architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/scope-check.md:31:`createEmptyProject()` creates backend-only default state with `P_H`, `P_V`, `HL_HV`, empty element arrays, empty dependency graph, and process root (`backend/src/models/Project.ts:67-120`). The active frontend initializes its world through `initializeWorld()` inside app-shell session flows instead (`frontend/src/application/appShell/ProjectSessionUseCases.ts:27-32`, `frontend/src/application/appShell/ProjectSessionUseCases.ts:96-110`).
./architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/validation/review-rg.stdout.log:49:architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/scope-check.md:35:`backend/src/server.ts` mounts `projectsRouter` at `/api/projects` (`backend/src/server.ts:1-15`). `backend/src/api/projects.ts` exposes list/create/get/update/delete route handlers (`backend/src/api/projects.ts:11-110`) backed by `ProjectRepository` (`backend/src/api/projects.ts:1-5`). Update accepts the request body as `updates` with no DTO validation beyond existence (`backend/src/api/projects.ts:65-77`). Error handlers use `error: any` (`backend/src/api/projects.ts:15-18`, `backend/src/api/projects.ts:35-38`, `backend/src/api/projects.ts:55-58`, `backend/src/api/projects.ts:78-84`, `backend/src/api/projects.ts:103-108`).
./architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/validation/review-rg.stdout.log:50:architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/scope-check.md:43:`backend/tests/integration/projects.spec.ts` tests `/api/projects` creation, loading, update, list, sort, and delete behavior (`backend/tests/integration/projects.spec.ts:39-342`). The tests assert backend DTO defaults such as `planes`, `hingeLines`, `elements2D`, `elements3D`, `dependencyGraph`, `processTree`, and `view2D` (`backend/tests/integration/projects.spec.ts:51-81`, `backend/tests/integration/projects.spec.ts:135-154`, `backend/tests/integration/projects.spec.ts:171-215`). They do not exercise frontend `ProjectService` command streams or the app-shell Drive flow.
./architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/validation/review-rg.stdout.log:51:architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/scope-check.md:47:`frontend/src/components/dialogs/OpenProjectDialog.vue` imports the runtime `projectService` and imports `ProjectMetadata` by reaching across the monorepo into backend implementation source: `import type { ProjectMetadata } from '../../../../backend/src/models/Project';` (`frontend/src/components/dialogs/OpenProjectDialog.vue:54-58`). It stores `projects` as `ProjectMetadata[]` (`frontend/src/components/dialogs/OpenProjectDialog.vue:68`) and calls `projectService.listProjects()` / `projectService.loadProject()` (`frontend/src/components/dialogs/OpenProjectDialog.vue:83-108`). Those methods do not exist on the current `frontend/src/services/ProjectService.ts`, which only exposes static command-stream serialization, validation, and deserialization (`frontend/src/services/ProjectService.ts:24-133`).
./architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/validation/review-rg.stdout.log:52:architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/scope-check.md:49:Search found no active source import of the component by component name; current app-shell UI renders `StartupDialog`, not `OpenProjectDialog` (`frontend/src/App.vue:1-16`, `frontend/src/App.vue:91-108`). Toolbar open-project emits to `runtime.actions.openProjectDialog` (`frontend/src/App.vue:26-32`), which only sets the StartupDialog visible (`frontend/src/application/appShell/AppShellRuntime.ts:137-145`, `frontend/src/application/appShell/ProjectSessionUseCases.ts:150-152`). Therefore the direct backend import leak is real in the source tree but appears attached to a dead dialog surface.
./architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/validation/review-rg.stdout.log:53:architecture-audit/wave-plan.md:441:- `backend/src/models/Project.ts`
./architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/validation/review-rg.stdout.log:54:architecture-audit/wave-plan.md:442:- `backend/src/api/projects.ts`
./architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/validation/review-rg.stdout.log:55:architecture-audit/wave-plan.md:445:- frontend direct backend import in `frontend/src/components/dialogs/OpenProjectDialog.vue`
./architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/validation/review-rg.stdout.log:56:architecture-audit/wave-plan.md:459:- Delete the direct frontend import from `backend/src/models/Project` regardless of chosen backend stance.
./architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/validation/review-rg.stdout.log:57:architecture-audit/baseline/quality-report.md:47:The backend `ProjectDTO` uses `Array<any>` for 2D and 3D elements, `root: any` for process-tree state, and `Array<any>` for command operations (`backend/src/models/Project.ts:13`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:14`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:42`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:50`). It therefore cannot independently validate the frontend command-sourced format described by `ProjectService` (`frontend/src/services/ProjectService.ts:261`, `frontend/src/services/ProjectService.ts:301`).
./architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/validation/review-rg.stdout.log:58:architecture-audit/baseline/quality-report.md:97:Backend integration tests exist for project API behavior (`backend/tests/integration/projects.spec.ts:7`, `backend/tests/integration/projects.spec.ts:9`), but the DTO accepts broad `any` fields for elements, process tree, and operations (`backend/src/models/Project.ts:13`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:14`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:42`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:50`). This limits the ability of backend tests to catch contract drift between frontend persistence and backend storage.
./architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/validation/review-rg.stdout.log:59:architecture-audit/baseline/quality-report.md:130:`OpenProjectDialog.vue` imports `ProjectMetadata` from `../../../../backend/src/models/Project` (`frontend/src/components/dialogs/OpenProjectDialog.vue:55`, `frontend/src/components/dialogs/OpenProjectDialog.vue:56`, `frontend/src/components/dialogs/OpenProjectDialog.vue:57`). This creates cross-workspace build coupling without establishing a shared contract package. The same dialog then uses the frontend `projectService` rather than backend HTTP routes (`frontend/src/components/dialogs/OpenProjectDialog.vue:56`, `frontend/src/components/dialogs/OpenProjectDialog.vue:68`), reinforcing that the import is a type leak rather than a clean API boundary.
./architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/validation/review-rg.stdout.log:60:architecture-audit/baseline/architecture-map.md:15:The backend entry point is `backend/src/server.ts`, which creates the Express app and port, installs CORS and JSON middleware, mounts `/health` and `/api/projects`, and starts listening (`backend/src/server.ts:6`, `backend/src/server.ts:7`, `backend/src/server.ts:10`, `backend/src/server.ts:11`, `backend/src/server.ts:14`, `backend/src/server.ts:15`, `backend/src/server.ts:18`). Its project routes use a file-backed repository directly inside the router module (`backend/src/api/projects.ts:1`, `backend/src/api/projects.ts:2`, `backend/src/api/projects.ts:4`, `backend/src/api/projects.ts:5`).
./architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/validation/review-rg.stdout.log:61:architecture-audit/baseline/architecture-map.md:55:The backend is a thin Express/file-storage stack. Routes directly instantiate `ProjectRepository` with `process.cwd()/data/projects` (`backend/src/api/projects.ts:4`, `backend/src/api/projects.ts:5`) and call repository methods in each route handler (`backend/src/api/projects.ts:11`, `backend/src/api/projects.ts:25`, `backend/src/api/projects.ts:45`, `backend/src/api/projects.ts:65`, `backend/src/api/projects.ts:91`). `ProjectDTO` is a broad DTO with `Array<any>` for frontend element snapshots, `root: any` for process tree, and `Array<any>` operations (`backend/src/models/Project.ts:6`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:13`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:14`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:42`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:50`). Backend persistence is therefore separate from the command-sourced frontend `ProjectService` rather than a shared contract layer.
./architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/validation/review-rg.stdout.log:62:architecture-audit/baseline/architecture-map.md:90:`OpenProjectDialog.vue` imports `ProjectMetadata` directly from backend source with a relative monorepo path (`frontend/src/components/dialogs/OpenProjectDialog.vue:55`, `frontend/src/components/dialogs/OpenProjectDialog.vue:56`, `frontend/src/components/dialogs/OpenProjectDialog.vue:57`, `frontend/src/components/dialogs/OpenProjectDialog.vue:68`). This is a frontend Vue component depending on backend implementation files rather than a shared API-contract package.
./architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/validation/review-rg.stdout.log:63:architecture-audit/baseline/architecture-map.md:92:Despite that type-only import, the active frontend persistence path is local/Drive-oriented: `App.vue` creates `ProjectService`/Drive flows, while `ProjectService` serializes command history and replays commands (`frontend/src/App.vue:160`, `frontend/src/App.vue:375`, `frontend/src/App.vue:416`, `frontend/src/App.vue:431`, `frontend/src/services/ProjectService.ts:261`, `frontend/src/services/ProjectService.ts:301`, `frontend/src/services/GoogleDriveService.ts:247`, `frontend/src/services/GoogleDriveService.ts:405`). The backend exposes Express project routes and a broad `ProjectDTO` (`backend/src/server.ts:14`, `backend/src/api/projects.ts:4`, `backend/src/api/projects.ts:11`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:6`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:13`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:50`), but the baseline found no normal frontend HTTP-client path using those project routes. The backend is therefore a parallel/disconnected persistence surface in the current architecture.
./architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/validation/review-rg.stdout.log:64:architecture-audit/baseline/domain-model.md:107:The backend has a separate DTO model that stores serialized element arrays, planes, hinge lines, commands, and process tree (`backend/src/models/Project.ts:6`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:13`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:14`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:22`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:46`) and seeds empty projects with P_H/P_V-style data (`backend/src/models/Project.ts:67`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:82`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:85`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:93`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:102`).
./architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/validation/review-rg.stdout.log:65:architecture-audit/baseline/inventory.md:58:HTTP API route handlers. `projects.ts` defines list/create/read/update/delete routes around `ProjectRepository` (`backend/src/api/projects.ts:4`, `backend/src/api/projects.ts:5`, `backend/src/api/projects.ts:11`, `backend/src/api/projects.ts:25`, `backend/src/api/projects.ts:45`, `backend/src/api/projects.ts:65`, `backend/src/api/projects.ts:91`); `health.ts` defines the health router (`backend/src/api/health.ts:3`).
./architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/validation/review-rg.stdout.log:66:architecture-audit/baseline/inventory.md:61:Backend DTO model definitions. `ProjectDTO` includes project metadata, serialized 2D/3D elements, planes, hinge lines, command history, and process tree (`backend/src/models/Project.ts:6`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:13`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:14`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:22`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:46`); `createEmptyProject()` seeds P_H/P_V-style initial data (`backend/src/models/Project.ts:67`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:82`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:85`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:93`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:102`).
