./architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/validation/review-round-02-grep.stdout.log:264:architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/validation/review-round-02-grep.stdout.log:97:architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/validation/review-rg.stdout.log:8:specs/001-dihedral-learning-mvp/plan.md:672:**Outputs**: `backend/src/api/projects.ts`, `frontend/src/services/ProjectService.ts`  
./architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/validation/review-round-02-grep.stdout.log:265:architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/validation/review-round-02-grep.stdout.log:98:architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/validation/review-rg.stdout.log:10:architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:21:- **The backend is not an adapter for that boundary.** It exposes `/api/projects` over a separate `ProjectDTO` shape (`backend/src/models/Project.ts:6-52`) and unvalidated file repository (`backend/src/storage/ProjectRepository.ts:27-95`).
./architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/validation/review-round-02-grep.stdout.log:266:architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/validation/review-round-02-grep.stdout.log:99:architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/validation/review-rg.stdout.log:12:architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:43:This would satisfy Wave 010 only if the backend becomes a real active boundary. It is not recommended for this wave because current app behavior is Drive-based, no frontend source fetches `/api/projects`, and adding a second storage adapter now would broaden scope toward product feature work rather than architectural deletion.
