./architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/validation/pre-implementation-reference-scan.stdout:249:./architecture-audit/baseline/inventory.md:54:### `backend/src/server.ts`
./architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/validation/pre-implementation-reference-scan.stdout:250:./architecture-audit/baseline/inventory.md:55:Express server entry point. It creates the Express app, configures CORS and JSON parsing, mounts health and project routers, and listens on a port from `PORT` or `3000`. Evidence: app and port creation (`backend/src/server.ts:6`, `backend/src/server.ts:7`), middleware (`backend/src/server.ts:10`, `backend/src/server.ts:11`), route mounting (`backend/src/server.ts:14`, `backend/src/server.ts:15`).
./architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/validation/pre-implementation-reference-scan.stdout:251:./architecture-audit/baseline/inventory.md:57:### `backend/src/api/`
./architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/validation/pre-implementation-reference-scan.stdout:252:./architecture-audit/baseline/inventory.md:58:HTTP API route handlers. `projects.ts` defines list/create/read/update/delete routes around `ProjectRepository` (`backend/src/api/projects.ts:4`, `backend/src/api/projects.ts:5`, `backend/src/api/projects.ts:11`, `backend/src/api/projects.ts:25`, `backend/src/api/projects.ts:45`, `backend/src/api/projects.ts:65`, `backend/src/api/projects.ts:91`); `health.ts` defines the health router (`backend/src/api/health.ts:3`).
./architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/validation/pre-implementation-reference-scan.stdout:253:./architecture-audit/baseline/inventory.md:60:### `backend/src/models/`
./architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/validation/pre-implementation-reference-scan.stdout:254:./architecture-audit/baseline/inventory.md:61:Backend DTO model definitions. `ProjectDTO` includes project metadata, serialized 2D/3D elements, planes, hinge lines, command history, and process tree (`backend/src/models/Project.ts:6`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:13`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:14`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:22`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:46`); `createEmptyProject()` seeds P_H/P_V-style initial data (`backend/src/models/Project.ts:67`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:82`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:85`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:93`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:102`).
./architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/validation/pre-implementation-reference-scan.stdout:255:./architecture-audit/baseline/inventory.md:63:### `backend/src/storage/`
./architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/validation/pre-implementation-reference-scan.stdout:256:./architecture-audit/baseline/inventory.md:64:File-backed persistence implementation. `FileStorage` is the low-level file storage class (`backend/src/storage/FileStorage.ts:7`, `backend/src/storage/FileStorage.ts:10`), and `ProjectRepository` wraps project persistence over a data directory (`backend/src/storage/ProjectRepository.ts:9`, `backend/src/storage/ProjectRepository.ts:12`).
./architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/validation/pre-implementation-reference-scan.stdout:257:./architecture-audit/baseline/domain-model.md:107:The backend has a separate DTO model that stores serialized element arrays, planes, hinge lines, commands, and process tree (`backend/src/models/Project.ts:6`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:13`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:14`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:22`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:46`) and seeds empty projects with P_H/P_V-style data (`backend/src/models/Project.ts:67`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:82`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:85`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:93`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:102`).
./architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/validation/pre-implementation-reference-scan.stdout:258:./architecture-audit/baseline/architecture-map.md:15:The backend entry point is `backend/src/server.ts`, which creates the Express app and port, installs CORS and JSON middleware, mounts `/health` and `/api/projects`, and starts listening (`backend/src/server.ts:6`, `backend/src/server.ts:7`, `backend/src/server.ts:10`, `backend/src/server.ts:11`, `backend/src/server.ts:14`, `backend/src/server.ts:15`, `backend/src/server.ts:18`). Its project routes use a file-backed repository directly inside the router module (`backend/src/api/projects.ts:1`, `backend/src/api/projects.ts:2`, `backend/src/api/projects.ts:4`, `backend/src/api/projects.ts:5`).
./architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/validation/pre-implementation-reference-scan.stdout:259:./architecture-audit/baseline/architecture-map.md:55:The backend is a thin Express/file-storage stack. Routes directly instantiate `ProjectRepository` with `process.cwd()/data/projects` (`backend/src/api/projects.ts:4`, `backend/src/api/projects.ts:5`) and call repository methods in each route handler (`backend/src/api/projects.ts:11`, `backend/src/api/projects.ts:25`, `backend/src/api/projects.ts:45`, `backend/src/api/projects.ts:65`, `backend/src/api/projects.ts:91`). `ProjectDTO` is a broad DTO with `Array<any>` for frontend element snapshots, `root: any` for process tree, and `Array<any>` operations (`backend/src/models/Project.ts:6`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:13`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:14`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:42`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:50`). Backend persistence is therefore separate from the command-sourced frontend `ProjectService` rather than a shared contract layer.
./architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/validation/pre-implementation-reference-scan.stdout:260:./architecture-audit/baseline/architecture-map.md:90:`OpenProjectDialog.vue` imports `ProjectMetadata` directly from backend source with a relative monorepo path (`frontend/src/components/dialogs/OpenProjectDialog.vue:55`, `frontend/src/components/dialogs/OpenProjectDialog.vue:56`, `frontend/src/components/dialogs/OpenProjectDialog.vue:57`, `frontend/src/components/dialogs/OpenProjectDialog.vue:68`). This is a frontend Vue component depending on backend implementation files rather than a shared API-contract package.
./architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/validation/pre-implementation-reference-scan.stdout:261:./architecture-audit/baseline/architecture-map.md:92:Despite that type-only import, the active frontend persistence path is local/Drive-oriented: `App.vue` creates `ProjectService`/Drive flows, while `ProjectService` serializes command history and replays commands (`frontend/src/App.vue:160`, `frontend/src/App.vue:375`, `frontend/src/App.vue:416`, `frontend/src/App.vue:431`, `frontend/src/services/ProjectService.ts:261`, `frontend/src/services/ProjectService.ts:301`, `frontend/src/services/GoogleDriveService.ts:247`, `frontend/src/services/GoogleDriveService.ts:405`). The backend exposes Express project routes and a broad `ProjectDTO` (`backend/src/server.ts:14`, `backend/src/api/projects.ts:4`, `backend/src/api/projects.ts:11`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:6`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:13`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:50`), but the baseline found no normal frontend HTTP-client path using those project routes. The backend is therefore a parallel/disconnected persistence surface in the current architecture.
./architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/validation/pre-implementation-reference-scan.stdout:262:./architecture-audit/baseline/quality-report.md:47:The backend `ProjectDTO` uses `Array<any>` for 2D and 3D elements, `root: any` for process-tree state, and `Array<any>` for command operations (`backend/src/models/Project.ts:13`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:14`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:42`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:50`). It therefore cannot independently validate the frontend command-sourced format described by `ProjectService` (`frontend/src/services/ProjectService.ts:261`, `frontend/src/services/ProjectService.ts:301`).
./architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/validation/pre-implementation-reference-scan.stdout:263:./architecture-audit/baseline/quality-report.md:97:Backend integration tests exist for project API behavior (`backend/tests/integration/projects.spec.ts:7`, `backend/tests/integration/projects.spec.ts:9`), but the DTO accepts broad `any` fields for elements, process tree, and operations (`backend/src/models/Project.ts:13`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:14`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:42`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:50`). This limits the ability of backend tests to catch contract drift between frontend persistence and backend storage.
./architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/validation/pre-implementation-reference-scan.stdout:264:./architecture-audit/baseline/quality-report.md:130:`OpenProjectDialog.vue` imports `ProjectMetadata` from `../../../../backend/src/models/Project` (`frontend/src/components/dialogs/OpenProjectDialog.vue:55`, `frontend/src/components/dialogs/OpenProjectDialog.vue:56`, `frontend/src/components/dialogs/OpenProjectDialog.vue:57`). This creates cross-workspace build coupling without establishing a shared contract package. The same dialog then uses the frontend `projectService` rather than backend HTTP routes (`frontend/src/components/dialogs/OpenProjectDialog.vue:56`, `frontend/src/components/dialogs/OpenProjectDialog.vue:68`), reinforcing that the import is a type leak rather than a clean API boundary.
./architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/validation/pre-implementation-reference-scan.stdout:265:./architecture-audit/baseline/risk-register.md:14:| 6 | Type contracts are too weak at key boundaries | High | Medium | `Record<string, any>` operation/DTO shapes (`frontend/src/commands/operations/IOperation.ts:136`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:13`) |
./architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/validation/pre-implementation-reference-scan.stdout:266:./architecture-audit/baseline/risk-register.md:86:**Evidence:** Operation parameters, outputs, and serialized-operation data are `Record<string, any>` / free-form fields (`frontend/src/commands/operations/IOperation.ts:118`, `frontend/src/commands/operations/IOperation.ts:128`, `frontend/src/commands/operations/IOperation.ts:134`, `frontend/src/commands/operations/IOperation.ts:136`, `frontend/src/commands/operations/IOperation.ts:160`). Projection-plane realizations use `world: any` (`frontend/src/domain/world/ProjectionPlane.ts:1428`, `frontend/src/domain/world/ProjectionPlane.ts:1436`, `frontend/src/domain/world/ProjectionPlane.ts:1689`, `frontend/src/domain/world/ProjectionPlane.ts:1747`). Backend `ProjectDTO` uses `Array<any>` and `root: any` (`backend/src/models/Project.ts:13`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:14`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:42`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:50`).
./architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/validation/pre-implementation-reference-scan.stdout:267:./architecture-audit/baseline/risk-register.md:122:**Evidence:** Root package declares `backend` as a workspace (`package.json:7`, `package.json:8`) but root `build`, `test`, and `lint` delegate only to frontend (`package.json:11`, `package.json:12`, `package.json:14`). Backend has separate build/test scripts (`backend/package.json:7`, `backend/package.json:8`, `backend/package.json:10`). Backend project routes and DTOs are independent of frontend `ProjectService` (`backend/src/api/projects.ts:4`, `backend/src/api/projects.ts:5`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:13`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:50`; `frontend/src/services/ProjectService.ts:70`, `frontend/src/services/ProjectService.ts:261`).
