./architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/decision.md:129:1. **Backend workspace closure requires implementation-time search.** If removing `/api/projects` leaves only a health/server placeholder, deletion is preferred; if a current non-project backend reason exists, it must be documented and must not include stale project-contract code.
./research/wave-010-project-contract/scout-summary.md:9:The current source tree still has a disconnected backend project CRUD/file-storage architecture and a frontend source import leak into backend models. After Wave 009, active frontend project lifecycle is routed through `AppShellRuntime`, `ProjectPersistencePort`, Google Drive ports, and frontend `ProjectService` command-stream persistence. The backend `ProjectDTO` is a stale parallel shape, not a shared contract.
./research/wave-010-project-contract/scout-summary.md:11:Recommended proposal: delete the unused backend project API/storage/model/tests and delete the dead `OpenProjectDialog.vue` import leak. If backend is kept, it must be rebuilt as a real validated adapter around the Wave 004 `ProjectData` command-stream contract and included in root validation; current evidence does not justify that scope.
./research/wave-010-project-contract/scout-summary.md:21:- Backend DTO has broad `any` fields and a different model from frontend persistence: `backend/src/models/Project.ts:6-52`.
./research/wave-010-project-contract/scout-summary.md:22:- Backend route/storage accepts and stores unvalidated JSON/partial DTOs: `backend/src/api/projects.ts:65-77`, `backend/src/storage/FileStorage.ts:28-52`, `backend/src/storage/ProjectRepository.ts:78-95`.
./research/wave-010-project-contract/scout-summary.md:26:- Direct frontend backend import remains only in stale `OpenProjectDialog.vue`: `frontend/src/components/dialogs/OpenProjectDialog.vue:54-58`.
./research/wave-010-project-contract/scout-summary.md:27:- Current `App.vue` renders `StartupDialog`, not `OpenProjectDialog`: `frontend/src/App.vue:1-16`, `frontend/src/App.vue:91-108`.
